cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "Weather-Aware Imbalanced Risk Prediction on Himalayan Expeditions"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction code for a retrospective, expedition-level fatality-risk
  classification pipeline combining weather-aware feature construction,
  sequential FOA-GWO hybrid metaheuristic feature selection, a comparison of six
  imbalance treatments, and post-hoc probability calibration, with a leakage
  ablation quantifying the effect of post-outcome archival fields.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/developerasalearner/Himalayan_Single_Run"

authors:
  - family-names: Palo
    given-names: Chinmaya Kumar
    affiliation: "Veer Surendra Sai University of Technology, Burla, Odisha, India"
    email: chinmayakumarpalo.official@gmail.com
  - family-names: Palo
    given-names: Tusharkanta
    affiliation: "Silicon University, Bhubaneswar, Odisha, India"
  - family-names: Behera
    given-names: Himansu Sekhar
    affiliation: "Veer Surendra Sai University of Technology, Burla, Odisha, India"

keywords:
  - imbalanced classification
  - hybrid feature selection
  - grey wolf optimizer
  - forest optimization algorithm
  - probability calibration
  - data leakage
  - retrospective risk classification

